# {{name}}

{{description}}

A Sophon channel adapter plugin that enables sending and receiving messages
through the {{Name}} platform.

## Implemented Interface

`IChannelAdapter` from `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions`

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `ConnectAsync` | Establishes connection to {{Name}} |
| `DisconnectAsync` | Gracefully closes the connection |
| `SendAsync` | Sends a message through {{Name}} |
| `TestConnectionAsync` | Performs a lightweight health check |
| `GetHealth` | Returns current connection status |
| `ExtractChatId` | Extracts chat identifier from inbound messages |
| `ValidateRecipient` | Validates recipient ID format |

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK
- `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions` NuGet package

### Build

```bash
dotnet build
```

### Configuration

When adding this channel in the Sophon Dashboard, you will need:

| Setting | Type | Required | Description |
|---------|------|----------|-------------|
| `apiToken` | Secret | Yes | Authentication token for {{Name}} |
| `endpoint` | String | No | Base URL for the {{Name}} API |

### Install

```bash
sophon plugins install ./{{Name}}.dll
```

Or copy the built DLL to the Sophon plugins directory.

## Development Guide

1. Implement the connection logic in `ConnectAsync`
2. Implement message sending in `SendAsync`
3. Wire up inbound message handling (see the commented `HandleIncomingMessage` example)
4. Implement `TestConnectionAsync` with a real health check
5. Test the full send/receive lifecycle

